  "findings": [
    "Upstream App::OnQuit emits quit before optional process_singleton cleanup; Browser::Shutdown notifies OnQuit before posting main-loop quit closure. Neither event proves actual OS process exit.",
    "Upstream WillRunMainMessageLoop supplies QuitWhenIdleClosure. PostMainMessageLoopRun includes utility shutdown, Node environment stop/reset and BrowserContext destruction. These are possible later boundaries, not observed blocked calls in natural reports.",
    "The profiling wait is compile-conditional; no evidence current binary enables it. Do not attribute failure to it.",
    "Historic Mach wait booleans cannot distinguish singleton cleanup, idle-loop wait, context teardown, AppKit, XPC, LaunchServices, or process termination. No causal call site established.",
    "No changes to main/Host/normal-close deadline, no app.exit workaround, no new shipped classifier. One normal new exit does not repair prior failure."
  ],
